{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusGaugeCurvatureHookColumn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnusGaugeCurvatureHookColumn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_curvature_eq_of_word_traces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_curvature_eq_of_word_traces","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusGaugeCurvatureHookColumn.lean#L71-L86","doc":"**The closed form, conditional on the per-word hook identity with a common twist.**\nSuppose every commutator-member word-trace is `c` times an elementary-symmetric value —\n`tr (ρσ_aσ_{a+1}) = c · E a` and `tr (ρσ_{a+1}σ_a) = c · F a` — with **one** scalar `c` for all\nof them (the common twist `q^{(L+2)(1−j)}`; common because every such word has length `L+2`).\nThen `tr (ρ · Σ_a [σ_a, σ_{a+1}]) = c · Σ_a (E a − F a)`, which is the reduced-Burau closed form\nfor the hook column of the gauge-invariant curvature (the `4/[2]_q²` prefactor restored\nexternally). Sorry-free; proves the implication only (`_of_` naming per `local/formalizer`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_curvature_eq_sum_word_traces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_curvature_eq_sum_word_traces","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusGaugeCurvatureHookColumn.lean#L57-L69","doc":"**Linearity: the curvature trace is a signed sum of word-traces.** For any `R`-linear\nfunctional `tr : A →ₗ[R] R`,\n`tr (ρ · Σ_a [σ_a, σ_{a+1}]) = Σ_a (tr (ρ σ_a σ_{a+1}) − tr (ρ σ_{a+1} σ_a))`.\nEach term on the right is the trace of a *word* two generators longer than `ρ`, which is what\nlets the reduced-Burau hook identity apply term by term. Sorry-free, unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.curvatureSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.curvatureSum","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusGaugeCurvatureHookColumn.lean#L50-L55","doc":"The second-order (projector) curvature as a sum of nearest-neighbour commutators of the\ngenerators `σ`, over the interior pairs `a = 0, …, m−1`: `Σ_a (σ_a σ_{a+1} − σ_{a+1} σ_a)`. The\noverall scalar `4/[2]_q²` of `Ω₂^P` is omitted — it is a constant that commutes with everything\nbelow and is restored at the end. ","signatureChunk":0}]}